cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use AgentKillChain in academic, policy, or safety evaluation work, please cite it using this metadata."
title: "AgentKillChain: Persistent Compromise Evaluation for Autonomous AI Agents"
authors:
  - family-names: "O'Connor"
    given-names: "Kevin"
repository-code: "https://github.com/KevinOBytes/AgentKillChain"
url: "https://github.com/KevinOBytes/AgentKillChain"
license: "MIT"
date-released: "2026-03-10"
version: "0.1.0-prototype"
keywords:
  - "AI safety"
  - "agent evaluation"
  - "prompt injection"
  - "memory poisoning"
  - "tool use"
  - "frontier model evaluation"
abstract: >-
  AgentKillChain is an open prototype benchmark for evaluating persistent
  compromise in simulated autonomous AI agents, including latent memory
  poisoning, context drift, toolchain confusion, and delayed activation
  behaviors relevant to frontier model safety evaluation.
